The error is correct: I cannot use a negative offset from a fixed-duration step. Coffee must start at a specific wall-clock time that makes it finish exactly when pancakes finish. Instead, I'll delay coffee's start using `programStartOffset` so that the brew finishes at the same moment as the pancake cooking.

**Calculation:**
- Pancakes track: mix-dry (5m) + beat-wet (5m) + combine (1m) + rest-batter (10m) + preheat-griddle (5m) + cook-pancakes (15m) = 41 minutes = 2460 seconds
- Coffee track: grind-brew-setup (3m) + brew-coffee (8m) = 11 minutes = 660 seconds
- Delay coffee start: 2460 - 660 = 1800 seconds = 30 minutes

